  "bandSplitMethod": "The Island Areas tables give marital status in coarse ages (25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-64, 65-84). Each coarse never-married and spouse-present count is split over the game's 5-year bands with weights from the territory's own PCT2 population, and the US ACS 2024 never-married and spouse-present shares by band shifted on the logit scale so the territory's coarse total is reproduced exactly.",
  "arrangementsNote": "Adults by band (PCT2), living alone (65+ and all ages), and households are exact. The 2020 Island Areas census has no living-arrangements-by-age table, so the child-of-householder, other-relatives, nonrelatives and partner splits across 18-34 / 35-64 apply US ACS 2024 age shares to the territory's own totals (P20 relationship counts less the children under 18 in P22)."
